.TITLE "mkdir"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Creates a new directory. It generates a folder at the specified path, allowing for better __organization__ of files.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**md**

.DIV "TLDR"
**mkdir name**
Creates a new directory with the specified name in the current path.
> __name__ the new directory name

**mkdir path\to\directory**
Creates a new directory at the specified path.
> __path\to\directory__ the target path

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __mkdir__ automatically creates any necessary parent directories in the path if they do not already exist. This is a common and efficient way to build deep directory structures in one command.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:dir** **windows:rmdir**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/mkdir__
